    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **34 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, mirroring the existing `AssignBulkSignupWarning` pattern (which likewise runs on both the create and read pipelines and sets a transient field the mapper reads).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Integer householdMemberCount` field with getter/setter, alongside the existing transient `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`AssignHouseholdMemberCount.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners sharing the owner's `householdId` (a null `householdId` is a household of one), and stores it on the owner. Household membership itself is still assigned by the existing `AssignHousehold`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules unchanged.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** and **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `householdMemberCount` step in after `bulkSignupWarning` and before `respond`, so the count is derived from current data on both create and read (with the appropriate `transaction` / `readonly-transaction` governance).\n\nThe tier is computed at response time from the live household size, so the third member of a shared household reads back as `GOLD`, while lone/small households retain their SILVER/BRONZE behavior.",
